[[2047,96,4,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The radio \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied directly\n(pins 7 of connector A) by the battery via the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and the maxifuse J/B1 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>It receives a supply when the ignition is\nswitched on (INT) (pin 4 of connector A) via the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>With the side lights switched on, the supply\nreaches pin 6 of connector A by means of the line coming from the\nswitch for the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , protected\nby the controls illumination fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse\nbox \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               ; the radionavigator controls are therefore lit\nup when the lide lights are switched on.</p><p>Pin 8 of connector A, on the other hand,\nis earthed (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Pin 5 of connector A is connected to the\ncontrol unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which controls the aerial built into the\nheated rear windscreen. The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is then connected\nto the radio by means of the specific aerial lead.</p><p>Pin 2 of connector A of\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              receives,\nas an input, a supply which acts as a signal recognising the presence\nof the Bose system.</p><p>The amplifier \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied directly\nby the battery via the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 C</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>It is then connected by a special line to\nthe radio \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               - pin 6 of connector C - which sends the signal\nto switch on the amplifier.</p><p>Connector B of\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              sends out signals\nto the &#x27;Bose&#x27; HIFI system amplifier \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which, in turn, is\nconnected to the speakers: \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[2047,96,32772,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The rear woofer speaker \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P92</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is outside\nthe amplifier located in the rear parcel shelf.</p>"],[2047,96,65540,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The rear woofer speaker \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P92</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is built\ninto the casing that also houses the amplifier.</p>"]]